.TH SOVEREIGN-MENU 1 "May 2026" "v1.0" "Sovereign Mesh Manual"
.SH NAME
sovereign-menu \- Interactive arrow-selectable mesh navigator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sovereign-menu
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sovereign-menu
is an interactive, terminal-based dashboard used to navigate the Sovereign Mesh. It provides a visual representation of all 10 mesh nodes and allows the operator to virtually "teleport" between them using arrow keys.
.SH INTERFACE
.TP
\fBNavigation\fR
Use the \fBUP\fR and \fBDOWN\fR arrow keys to cycle through the available nodes.
.TP
\fBSelection\fR
Press \fBENTER\fR to select a node. This initiates the mind-segment teleportation protocol via \fBmesh_control.sh\fR.
.TP
\fBExit\fR
Press \fBq\fR to exit the navigator and return to the standard shell.
.SH TOPOLOGY
The navigator tracks the status of:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBBackbone Nodes:\fR Anchor, Forge, Sentry, Ops.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBEdge Nodes:\fR Relay, Capicant.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPhased Nodes:\fR Tokyo, Mumbai, Garland.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBLocal Node:\fR Aurora.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Requires a terminal window with at least 15 lines of height for stable rendering.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgmudd\fR(8), \fBmesh_control.sh\fR(8), \fBsovereign-auto\fR(1)
.SH AUTHOR
Sovereign Mesh Core Developers
